    "sourceGaps": [
      "1995E1: Anton Sirota (editor), *The Competition Problems from the International Chemistry Olympiads*, Volume2, IUVENTA, Bratislava,2009. Attributed compiler/teaching edition with printed teaching-copy conditions and commercial restriction. The obtained compilation prints no solution for this practical problem, no assignment of the actual A–E samples, no numerical marking rubric and no separate answer sheet. These missing materials are not supplied editorially.",
      "1995E2: Anton Sirota (editor), *The Competition Problems from the International Chemistry Olympiads*, Volume2, IUVENTA, Bratislava,2009. Attributed compiler/teaching edition with printed teaching-copy conditions and commercial restriction. This key lists required measurements and equations, but supplies no actual product mass or experimental yield, no hydration-number result and no obtained separate student report/answer sheet. The original wording “monometric” is retained. The printed product formula in the glycine reaction has NH rather than NH2; this discrepancy is retained rather than chemically corrected. No absent data are invented.",
      "1995E3: Anton Sirota (editor), *The Competition Problems from the International Chemistry Olympiads*, Volume2, IUVENTA, Bratislava,2009. Attributed compiler/teaching edition with printed teaching-copy conditions and commercial restriction. The source literally calls sulfuric acid “as indicator”, and prints coefficient1 before iodine in the iodate equation. Those native discrepancies are retained. The accurate iodate bottle concentration, actual titration volumes, product mass, copper percentage, hydration number and separate answer sheet are not obtained. This brief key is not a completed experimental dataset."
    ],
